From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: drm/msm/dsi: do not re-set link clock rates for every command

msm_dsi_host_xfer_prepare() called link_clk_set_rate() before every DSI
command. On MSM8916 the 28nm-lp PLL delivers 398322656 Hz for a requested
398358000 Hz, so the clock core treats every call as a change and relocks
the DSI PLL while video scan-out is running. Each backlight update (a DCS
write) then corrupts the picture. Only set the rates while the host is not
yet powered on; afterwards they are already correct.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/dsi_host.c
@@ -2175,7 +2175,15 @@
 	 * mdp clock need to be enabled to receive dsi interrupt
 	 */
 	pm_runtime_get_sync(&msm_host->pdev->dev);
-	cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
+	/*
+	 * Once the host is powered on the link clocks already run at the mode's
+	 * rates. Setting them again for every command is not a no-op when the
+	 * PLL cannot hit the requested rate exactly (MSM8916 28nm-lp: 398358000
+	 * requested, 398322656 delivered): the clock core reprograms the DSI
+	 * PLL mid-frame and video mode panels glitch on every backlight change.
+	 */
+	if (!msm_host->power_on)
+		cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_set_rate(msm_host);
 	cfg_hnd->ops->link_clk_enable(msm_host);
 
 	/* TODO: vote for bus bandwidth */
